<title>DENMARK: EU grants 1.6 bln Dkk loan facility to Oeresund.</title>
<headline>EU grants 1.6 bln Dkk loan facility to Oeresund.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish-Swedish Oeresundskonsortiet said on Thursday the European Union (EU) granted it a 1.6 billion crown loan facility for its road-rail, tunnel-bridge fixed link Oeresund project.</p>
<p>&quot;Derived from the European Coal &amp; Steel Union, the value of the facility corresponds to the expected cost of the steel supplied for the Oeresund project's coast to coast section and the Danish landworks,&quot; Oeresundskonsortiet said in a statement.</p>
<p>It said the interest and maturity would be negotiated prior to the possible draw-down of the loan.</p>
<p>The fixed link across the narrow Baltic sound between east Denmark and south Sweden is due for completion in the year 2000.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-339696</p>
</text>
